  <prompt>Owner 2026-11-25: "Continue with next tasks". Issue #2775 (gh issue view 2775) and DI-151 in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/defer-issues.md. `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationArrivedProducer.cs` `ThreadColumns` (~106) appends `RegardingFieldMap.AllRegardingFields`, which includes `sprk_regardingreportcard`; `sprk_communicationthread` has no such column, so the thread read (~182 `RetrieveAsync`) faults and every arrival notification is treated as private (under-fans, no deep link). `CommunicationThreadReadService.cs` (~51-56, `ThreadRegardingFields`) already excludes that column for the same reason. Search by name; origin/master.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE backend developer: .NET 10 BFF (Communication, Microsoft Graph SDK).</role>
  <goal>The arrival producer reads only columns that exist on sprk_communicationthread, so a thread with a regarding record notifies its normal audience and deep-links to the regarding record; privacy behaviour for a genuinely private thread is unchanged.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Reuse, do not fork: one definition of "the regarding lookups the thread has" used by both CommunicationThreadReadService and the producer (hoist it next to RegardingFieldMap or expose it from one of them). Pair the column list with the real schema (project testing rule): a test that the thread column list matches src/dataverse/solutions/SpaarkeMaster/Entities/sprk_CommunicationThread/Entity.xml (or the existing schema-agreement guard pattern), so a new regarding field on communication but not thread is caught. Read why a failed read means "private" and keep that fail-closed behaviour for a real read failure.</background>
  </context>
